WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.470
An AI broke

00:00:01.282 --> 00:00:02.814
ciphers experts never

00:00:02.626 --> 00:00:03.262
cracked

00:00:03.798 --> 00:00:04.965
MiniMax says an

00:00:04.777 --> 00:00:06.239
internal research model

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:07.217
produced the first

00:00:07.029 --> 00:00:08.444
practical attacks on

00:00:08.256 --> 00:00:09.859
several NIST competition

00:00:09.671 --> 00:00:10.873
candidates that had

00:00:10.685 --> 00:00:11.934
no known practical

00:00:11.746 --> 00:00:12.453
breaks

00:00:12.982 --> 00:00:13.783
It found full

00:00:13.595 --> 00:00:15.399
collisions in SHA-3

00:00:15.211 --> 00:00:17.404
candidate Blender-256

00:00:17.215 --> 00:00:18.029
in seconds

00:00:18.076 --> 00:00:18.984
and shrank a

00:00:18.796 --> 00:00:20.222
LOCKER solver matrix

00:00:20.034 --> 00:00:21.590
from 42 petabytes

00:00:21.425 --> 00:00:22.934
to 58 megabytes

00:00:23.462 --> 00:00:24.428
It also found

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.112
over a dozen

00:00:24.948 --> 00:00:26.197
unreported bugs in

00:00:26.009 --> 00:00:26.858
reference code

00:00:27.012 --> 00:00:28.367
including one typo

00:00:28.191 --> 00:00:28.851
that let it

00:00:28.662 --> 00:00:30.242
forge signatures using

00:00:30.101 --> 00:00:31.009
only the public

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:31.339
key

00:00:31.878 --> 00:00:32.892
Full story on

00:00:32.703 --> 00:00:33.599
the dashboard
